{"id":"b3c8bda61bc135a4","group":"58","path":"58/batch09/58-thm-jordan-curve.md","title":"Jordan Curve Theorem","display":"thm-jordan-curve — Jordan Curve Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-jordan-curve","aliases":["58-thm-jordan-curve"],"display":"thm-jordan-curve — Jordan Curve Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-jordan-curve]]","[[58-df-connected]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-jordan-curve"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-jordan-curve</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-jordan-curve — Jordan Curve Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"21c089d664e60689\" href=\"?note=21c089d664e60689\" title=\"58-df-jordan-curve\">58-df-jordan-curve</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"71801f5b9407391a\" href=\"?note=71801f5b9407391a\" title=\"58-df-connected\">58-df-connected</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\gamma,\\tau_{S^1},\\tau_{\\mathbb R^2},Y,\\tau_Y\\in V\">\\(\\gamma,\\tau_{S^1},\\tau_{\\mathbb R^2},Y,\\tau_Y\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{JordanCurve}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{JordanCurve}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"21c089d664e60689\" href=\"?note=21c089d664e60689\" title=\"58-df-jordan-curve\">58-df-jordan-curve</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Connected}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Connected}_S\\)</span> is the two-place predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"71801f5b9407391a\" href=\"?note=71801f5b9407391a\" title=\"58-df-connected\">58-df-connected</a> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Components}\">\\(\\operatorname{Components}\\)</span> is the set-valued term defined below</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}jordan\\text{-}components}\\vdash\\operatorname{Components}(Y,\\tau_Y)\\coloneqq\\left\\{C\\subseteq Y:C\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\mathrm{Connected}_S(C,\\{C\\cap U:U\\in\\tau_Y\\})\\land\\forall D\\subseteq Y\\;\\bigl(C\\subseteq D\\land\\mathrm{Connected}_S(D,\\{D\\cap U:U\\in\\tau_Y\\})\\to D=C\\bigr)\\right\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}jordan\\text{-}components}\\vdash\\operatorname{Components}(Y,\\tau_Y)\\coloneqq\\left\\{C\\subseteq Y:C\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\mathrm{Connected}_S(C,\\{C\\cap U:U\\in\\tau_Y\\})\\land\\forall D\\subseteq Y\\;\\bigl(C\\subseteq D\\land\\mathrm{Connected}_S(D,\\{D\\cap U:U\\in\\tau_Y\\})\\to D=C\\bigr)\\right\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}jordan\\text{-}curve} \\vdash \\mathrm{JordanCurve}_S(\\gamma,\\tau_{S^1},\\tau_{\\mathbb R^2})\\to\\left\\lvert\\operatorname{Components}\\!\\left(\\mathbb R^2\\setminus\\gamma[S^1],\\{(\\mathbb R^2\\setminus\\gamma[S^1])\\cap U:U\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^2}\\}\\right)\\right\\rvert=2\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}jordan\\text{-}curve} \\vdash \\mathrm{JordanCurve}_S(\\gamma,\\tau_{S^1},\\tau_{\\mathbb R^2})\\to\\left\\lvert\\operatorname{Components}\\!\\left(\\mathbb R^2\\setminus\\gamma[S^1],\\{(\\mathbb R^2\\setminus\\gamma[S^1])\\cap U:U\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^2}\\}\\right)\\right\\rvert=2\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Connected components are expanded as maximal connected subspaces, so no untyped local <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi_0\">\\(\\pi_0\\)</span> operator remains.</li>\n<li>The complement of the image of a Jordan curve has exactly two connected components.</li>\n<li>The bounded component is the interior and the unbounded component is the exterior; the curve is their common boundary.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-jordan-curve","status":"resolved","id":"21c089d664e60689","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-jordan-curve]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-connected","status":"resolved","id":"71801f5b9407391a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-connected]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-jordan-curve","status":"resolved","id":"21c089d664e60689","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{JordanCurve}_S\\subseteq V^3$ (see [[58-df-jordan-curve]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-connected","status":"resolved","id":"71801f5b9407391a","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Connected}_S$ is the two-place predicate from [[58-df-connected]] and $\\operatorname{Components}$ is the set-valued term defined below","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\gamma,\\tau_{S^1},\\tau_{\\mathbb R^2},Y,\\tau_Y\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{JordanCurve}_S\\subseteq V^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Connected}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Components}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}jordan\\text{-}components}\\vdash\\operatorname{Components}(Y,\\tau_Y)\\coloneqq\\left\\{C\\subseteq Y:C\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\mathrm{Connected}_S(C,\\{C\\cap U:U\\in\\tau_Y\\})\\land\\forall D\\subseteq Y\\;\\bigl(C\\subseteq D\\land\\mathrm{Connected}_S(D,\\{D\\cap U:U\\in\\tau_Y\\})\\to D=C\\bigr)\\right\\}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}jordan\\text{-}curve} \\vdash \\mathrm{JordanCurve}_S(\\gamma,\\tau_{S^1},\\tau_{\\mathbb R^2})\\to\\left\\lvert\\operatorname{Components}\\!\\left(\\mathbb R^2\\setminus\\gamma[S^1],\\{(\\mathbb R^2\\setminus\\gamma[S^1])\\cap U:U\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^2}\\}\\right)\\right\\rvert=2","display":true},{"tex":"\\pi_0","display":false}],"bytes":1524,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4244","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-thm-jordan-curve.md|58-thm-jordan-curve]]（batch09）"}],"outgoing":["21c089d664e60689","71801f5b9407391a"]}